A||||6||JohnnyK||Undercoating||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||11-18-2000||02:43 PM||||My 85 SE is pretty rusty (enough that part of the cradle snapped. Where the a-arm connects to it). But I welded that back, and I want to drive it throughout the winter. What is a better method of rust prevention? Just undercoating with oil, or getting some of that tar/asphalt (I don't know what it is) stuff and painting that on?||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-18-2000||03:03 PM||||Try the stuff in the spray cans...it seems to work pretty well and it sticks even if you apply it in cold weather.<P>Just be sure the cans are room temp. before you spray the stuff on. And be sure what you're applying it to is fairly clean and dry.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||11-18-2000||09:22 PM||||you need to treat the rust. any of the products that convert rust into an inert coating should work. (rustolium makes one)just covering it won't stop it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||11-19-2000||08:50 PM||||After you stop the rusting process you should paint the parts not undercoat them. That undercoating stuff is crap and traps water between the part and the undercoat causing more damage, and you won't see it until it's to late. Use Rustoleum Rusty Metal primer and than black paint.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tom88gt||11-19-2000||08:56 PM||||If your car is that rusty, you may want to consider buying a clean one.  Fieros typically have a poor market value and you can probably find a clean rust free one for a lot less than repairing yours.  370,000 made and most that are still driving can be bought cheap (except from the 1600+ Fiero-holics on the Forum).||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnnyK||11-19-2000||09:05 PM||||I was going to put a new cradle on it, but screw it. I might do that later if this one breaks (already did once, had to go welding..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> It snapped in the frame where the a-arm connects. Good thing that didn't happen at highway speed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
